ine &#x0002b; sulfadoxine&#x02013;pyrimethamine, mefloquine &#x0002b; artesunate and artemether &#x0002b; lumefantrine combination therapies to treat <named-content content-type="genus-species">Plasmodium falciparum</named-content> malaria in the Chittagong Hill Tracts, Bangladesh</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>99</volume><fpage>727</fpage><lpage>735</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16095643</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050169-b029"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Hamour</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Melaku</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Keus</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wambugu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Atkin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Malaria in the Nuba Mountains of Sudan: Baseline genotypic resistance and efficacy of the artesunate plus sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine and artesunate plus amodiaquine combinations</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>99</volume><fpage>548</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15869770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050169-b030"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Checchi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Roddy</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamara</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Morineau</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Evidence basis for antimalarial policy change in Sierra Leone: Five in vivo efficacy studies of chloroquine, sulphadoxine-pyrimethamine and amodiaquine</article-title><source>Trop Med Int Health</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>146</fpage><lpage>153</lpage><pub-id pub-id-ty